ours he has to work is 20? Then he's only working 18 hours, so 18 hours at $20 per hour? That seems too simple. But maybe there's a misunderstanding here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe there's a problem with the way the hours are phrased. Maybe he has 20 hours left in the week after working 18, meaning the total time is 20 hours, so he's only working 18? But 18 hours to work would mean earning 18 * 20. But maybe the problem is that he has 10 + 8 = 18 hours already, and 20 - 18 = 2 hours left. So he'll work 18 hours and 2 hours. So total hours are 20. Therefore, his earnings would be 18 hours * $20 plus 2 hours * $20. Let me compute that.\n\nFirst, 18 hours is 18 * $20, and 2 hours is 2 * $20. So total earnings would be 18*20 + 2*20. Which is 20*(18 + 2) = 20*20 = $400. Therefore, the answer should be $\\boxed{400}$.\n\nBut let me make sure I didn't misinterpret anything. Maybe the question is phrased differently. Another way to think: If he has 20 hours left in the week, and he has already worked 18 hours (10 + 8), then he has 2 left. So total hours is 18 + 2 = 20. Hence, earnings would be 20 hours * $20 = $400. That matches the answer. So the final answer should be \\boxed{400}.\n</think>\n\n\\boxed{400}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?", "answer": "The total number of hours that Rafael has worked by Tuesday is 8+10 = <<8+10=18>>18 hours.\nTo complete his assigned work hours, Rafael works 20 hours more, making his total weekly hours to be 18+20 = <<38=38>>38 hours.\nSince he is paid $20 per hour, he makes $20*38 = $<<20*38=760>>760 a week.\n#### 760", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rafael works 10 hours on Monday and 8 hours on Tuesday on his delivery job. With 20 hours left to work in the week, how much money does Rafael make if he is paid $20 per hour?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["760"], "solution": "760"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 389, 806, 9691, 2618, 13, 3085, 220, 17, 15, 4115, 2115, 311, 975, 304, 279, 2003, 11, 1246, 1753, 3220, 1558, 54400, 1281], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 54400, 4278, 220, 16, 15, 4115, 389, 7014, 323, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 7589, 11, 892, 11367, 705, 311, 220, 16, 23, 4115, 773, 3041, 13, 2619, 525, 220, 17, 15, 4115, 2115, 304, 279, 2003, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 2790, 882, 566, 702, 311, 975, 374, 220, 16, 23, 4115, 5519, 220, 17, 4115, 566]}
