ich is boxed as \\boxed{15}.\n\nBut let me check again. Thursday has 12 total, Friday has 13. Total is 25. Brown is 20%, so 25*(20/100) = 5. Same for green. Then yellow leaves = 25 - 5 -5 = 15. Yep, that seems correct. So the final answer is 15.\n</think>\n\nThe total number of leaves collected is $12 + 13 = 25$. 20% of 25 leaves are brown and green, which equal $25 \\times 0.2 = 5$ each. The remaining yellow leaves are $25 - 5 - 5 = 15$. \n\n\\boxed{15}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Bronson decides to collect Oak Leaves from around his Neighborhood. He collects 12 on Thursday and 13 on Friday. 20% are Brown and 20% are Green. The rest are yellow. How many yellow leaves does he collect?", "answer": "He collects 25 leaves because 12 + 13 = <<12+13=25>>25\n60% of them are yellow because 100 - 20 - 20 = <<100-20-20=60>>60\nHe collects 15 yellow leaves because 25 x .6 = <<25*.6=15>>15\n#### 15", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Bronson decides to collect Oak Leaves from around his Neighborhood. He collects 12 on Thursday and 13 on Friday. 20% are Brown and 20% are Green. The rest are yellow. How many yellow leaves does he collect?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["15"], "solution": "15"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 19820, 930, 27627, 311, 6530, 18283, 77514, 504, 2163, 806, 61512, 13, 1260, 51207, 220, 16, 17, 389, 7794, 323, 220, 16, 18, 389, 6602, 13, 220, 17, 15, 4, 525, 10471, 323, 220, 17, 15, 4], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 419, 3491, 700, 13, 2055, 11, 19820, 930, 51207, 10901, 916, 1378, 2849, 25, 7794, 323, 6602, 13, 1913, 7794, 566, 51207, 220, 16, 17, 10901, 11, 323, 389, 6602, 566, 51207, 220, 16, 18, 10901, 13, 5005, 1052, 525, 53108, 25, 220, 17, 15, 4, 525, 10471, 11,