n\nSo, current time is 4 months from now? Or from when? The problem says \"currently, she was able to return half...\", and asks \"how much will she still... 4 months from now?\"\n\nSo, perhaps the timeline is: Initially borrowed 6 months ago. Now, she has half the amount. Then, how does she pay the money? If she has 6 months repaid, then now she has half the amount. Therefore, the remaining amount is half again. Therefore, if she has half, then 4 months from now, she has her next 4 months. Therefore, the total amount is going to be half the original amount, but with 4 months left. So, maybe the answer is (original amount borrowed - 60) plus (4*10) = 120 - 60 + 40 = 100, which is double the amount. Therefore, she will owe her brother 100 dollars.\n\nBut the problem", "source_record": {"question": "Shara borrowed money from her brother 6 months ago. She returned $10 per month to her brother. Currently, she was able to return half of the money she borrowed. How much will she still owe her brother 4 months from now?", "answer": "For 6 months, Shara was able to return $10 x 6 = $<<10*6=60>>60 to her brother.\nSince she already returned half of the money, then this means she currently owes her brother $<<60=60>>60.\nFour months from now, she will be able to pay an additional $10 x 4 = $<<10*4=40>>40.\nThus, she will still owe her brother $60 - $40 = $<<60-40=20>>20 four months from now.\n#### 20", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Shara borrowed money from her brother 6 months ago. She returned $10 per month to her brother. Currently, she was able to return half of the money she borrowed. How much will she still owe her brother 4 months from now?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["20"], "solution": "20"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 1417, 505