f of that is 2. Adding 12 + 2 gives 14. Yes, that seems right. The answer should be in a box, so \\boxed{14}.\n</think>\n\nThe total number of matches Brendan won is calculated by adding the matches won in the first two rounds and the half of the matches in the last round. \n\n- Matches in the first two rounds: $2 \\times 6 = 12$\n- Matches in the last round: Half of 4 matches is 2\n\nAdding both results: $12 + 2 = 14$\n\n\\boxed{14}<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071, 2348, 5248, 74424, 13, 1260, 14816, 678, 315, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 220, 17, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 14816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700,